  "caveats": [
    "joint -> single keeps the spouse's income attached; the frozen table has zero non-joint filers with spouse income, so that direction is extrapolation and is reported but never quoted as a finding.",
    "'Flip exactly one' means one reader-facing attribute. marital_status necessarily moves filing_status with it, and dependents moves famsize, because those pairs are structurally inseparable in this data.",
    "A twin gap is what the MODEL does when one attribute moves. It is evidence about a fitted function, not a causal estimate of tax law."
  ]
